<p>In the kneeling lunge, push the hips gently forward and down rather than arching your lower back to fake depth - the stretch should live in the front of the rear hip. In the side bend, reach up and over without twisting. In the side lunge, keep the extended leg's foot flat and sit back into the bent side. In the runner's stretch, use your hands on the floor for support and let each exhale take you slightly lower.</p>
<p>Ten days of lunging earned your hips this - give each side its full, unhurried pass.</p>
<p><strong>Make it Harder:</strong> Not the point on a rest day - sink a little deeper with every exhale and let the counts stretch longer instead.</p>
<p><strong>Make it Easier:</strong> Shorten every stance - a smaller lunge is the same stretch with a gentler dose.</p>
