<p>Day 16 hands the turtle to your upper body. Straight sets, 60 seconds rest, 4 sets each: 10 chest expansions, 12 W-extensions, a 30-count chest squeeze and 12 tricep extensions. The card's tempo rule applies to the three moving exercises - a 3-count in each direction, arms tense the whole way - while the chest squeeze, already an exercise in going nowhere, simply runs its longer 30-count.</p>
<p>Slow tempo does something specific to unweighted arm work: it closes the loophole. At normal speed, exercises like chest expansions can coast on swing - the arms travel, the muscles barely register. At a 3-count out and a 3-count back, with deliberate tension held throughout, the same arc becomes six seconds of continuous work per rep, and the rear shoulders and upper back have to fund every one of them. That is why expansions dropped to 10 reps: the currency changed. W-extensions and tricep extensions follow the same rule overhead, and the squeeze anchors the middle of the session with tension that never moves at all.</p>
